course: dictionary
lesson: 4459
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can find the right one by reading the words around it. «The boats sailed out of the harbour at dawn.» Here a harbour is a place by the sea where boats stay safe from waves and storms.
explain: Now read this: «The family harboured the lost puppy for a week.» Harbour is being used as a verb here, and it means to hide or keep someone. Check it: a place for boats would not fit this sentence, so the meaning must be different.
explain: Words can also describe feelings. «She harboured a secret hope that her brother would come home.» To harbour a feeling is to keep it inside for a long time. When you meet a familiar word in a new place, ask yourself: does my first meaning still make sense here?
fact: A harbour is a place by the sea where boats and ships stay safe.
fact: To harbour someone is to hide or keep them, often someone hiding from others.
fact: To harbour a feeling is to keep it for a long time.
fact: «Taronga Zoo sits on a hill above the harbour» in Sydney, so harbour can also be a name for a place.
fact: Harbour is also spelled harbor in American English, but the meaning is the same.
exercise: «Ships sailed out of the harbour at dawn.» What is a harbour? | A river that runs through a forest | A tall hill above the town | A kind of fish | *A place by the sea where boats stay safe
exercise: In a maths problem, boats arrive in the harbour and boats leave the harbour. What do you do? | *Add the boats that arrive and take away the boats that leave | Add all the boats, both arriving and leaving | Take away the boats that arrive | Multiply the boats by the number of ships
exercise: «The old fisher harboured a hope that his son would return.» What does harboured mean here? | Painted | *Kept for a long time | Washed clean by the waves
test: «The family harboured the lost puppy until its owner was found.» What does harboured mean? | *Kept it safe and hidden | Sold it to a shop | Ran away from it | Fed it once and forgot it
test: «Taronga Zoo sits on a hill above the harbour.» What kind of place is the harbour here? | *A place by the sea where boats stay safe | A school | A dark cave | A bakery
exam: «Cities grew at useful spots: where a harbour was sheltered.» According to the text, why did cities grow at these spots? | Because the roads were all straight | Because of tsunamis | *Because a sheltered harbour was useful | Because the zoos were there
